# C014 independent review obligations

Finite P/N, known nonempty alphabet, disjoint ownership blocks, unconstrained
regular factors, all component counts, noiseless full-word labels are essential.

1. Check that nonzero count sets plus positive-presence counts represent C_a
   exactly, especially zeros, empty P/N, epsilon, duplicates and m=1. Confirm
   contradictory labels are rejected even if some other negative fails the
   predicate. No early fallback bypasses remaining validation.
2. Check quantifier order: each n must have a single symbol distinguishing its
   count from every positive's count. Different symbols may reject different
   negatives. When all negatives pass, singleton finite languages fit the
   sample. Closing regular factors under block merging gives all partitions.
   Conversely singleton compatibility forces this condition.
3. Verify sparse absent-symbol scanning visits at most support(n)+1 entries.
   This is an operation-count argument for expected hash tables; it is not
   a whole-program or arbitrary-bit-cost linear-time guarantee.
4. Verify Stirling recurrence, Bell(m-1) pair counts, m=1 boundary, two witness
   IDs, original-index certificates and representative-language rule. Compact
   witnesses must reject every negative and accept every positive.
5. Check frozen C010 exact source path/hash, original data/deadline forwarding,
   disabled enumeration, preserved native payload, and honest incomplete/error
   normalization. A false predicate invokes exact search, never a guessed
   singleton or physical partition.
6. Auditor should compare exact full families on small cases by independent
   RGS enumeration, replay certificates/witness rules, and include countmix
   P={ab,aabb}, N={aab}, contradictory labels, empty P/N and epsilon controls.
   Reuse bounded C013 long cases only after source/protocol static GO. Charge
   parsing, count work, output serialization and external wall/memory; compare
   different compact/expanded output contracts honestly. No test was run here.
